WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:30.040
Alice's Adventures in Wonderland by Lewis Carroll. Copyright Blackcat Publishing

00:32.040 --> 00:36.500
Chapter 1 The White Rabbit

00:36.920 --> 00:38.600
It is a sunny afternoon.

00:39.120 --> 00:41.950
Alice and her sister are sitting by the river.

00:42.000 --> 00:46.205
Alice's sister is reading a book with no pictures.

00:46.400 --> 00:52.000
'I don't like books without any pictures.' Alice thinks.
  
00:52.100 --> 00:53.500
She is sleepy.

00:53.600 --> 00:56.670
Just then she sees a White Rabbit.

00:57.000 --> 01:01.100
He looks at his watch and says, 'I'm late.'
  
01:01.200 --> 01:04.730
'How strange!' Alice thinks.

01:04.800 --> 01:07.500
'A rabbit with a watch!'

01:07.600 --> 01:12.400
She follows the rabbit across the grass and into a big hole.

01:12.500 --> 01:15.500
She falls slowly down the hole.

01:15.600 --> 01:19.000
Then she stops falling and stands up.

01:19.100 --> 01:21.200
She looks around.

01:21.320 --> 01:25.150
Alice sees the rabbit again and follows him.

01:25.250 --> 01:29.630
He is running around a hall with a lot of doors.

01:29.760 --> 01:34.720
Then she sees a glass table with a small key on it.

01:34.840 --> 01:40.300
She takes the key and tries to open the doors, but she can't.

01:40.400 --> 01:45.160
Then she sees a very small door and opens it.

01:45.200 --> 01:48.000
There is a beautiful garden.

01:48.180 --> 01:52.230
I want to go into that garden. Thinks Alice.
 
01:52.240 --> 01:54.820
But I'm too big.

01:54.900 --> 01:59.700
She puts the key on the glass table and sees a bottle on it.

01:59.800 --> 02:03.200
It says, drink me on the bottle.

02:03.300 --> 02:06.900
She takes the bottle and drinks it all.

02:07.000 --> 02:15.800
Oh, how strange. She says. Now I'm very small and I can go into the garden.
 
02:16.400 --> 02:20.990
But the door is closed and the key is on the table.

02:21.000 --> 02:25.350
She is too small now and she can't get the key.

02:25.360 --> 02:29.750
She is very sad and starts to cry.

02:29.760 --> 02:34.150
Alice sees a small glass box under the table.

02:34.160 --> 02:40.030
Inside the box there is a cake with the words, eat me on it.

02:40.040 --> 02:43.640
I'm going to eat it, says Alice.

02:43.880 --> 02:47.385
Perhaps I can grow and take the key from the table.

02:47.500 --> 02:51.220
She eats the cake, but nothing happens.

02:51.300 --> 02:54.410
Then suddenly she becomes big.

02:54.500 --> 02:59.030
Now I can get the key. She thinks.
 
02:59.160 --> 03:03.370
She takes the key and goes to the door to the garden.

03:03.450 --> 03:06.890
But she is too big and can't go in.

03:07.000 --> 03:10.930
She sits down and starts to cry again.

03:11.000 --> 03:13.670
Her tears make a big pool.

03:13.720 --> 03:17.615
Suddenly she sees the White Rabbit again.

03:17.710 --> 03:24.870
He is wearing a lovely jacket and he has got white gloves in one hand and flowers in the other.
  
03:24.920 --> 03:29.635
Oh, the Duchess is going to be angry because I'm late.

03:29.720 --> 03:31.600
Says the White Rabbit.

03:32.000 --> 03:35.390
Excuse me, sir. Says Alice.
 
03:35.450 --> 03:39.100
The White Rabbit is afraid and runs away.

03:39.200 --> 03:42.500
His white gloves fall to the floor.

03:42.550 --> 03:49.190
Alice looks at her hand and she is suddenly wearing one of the White Rabbit's gloves.

03:49.200 --> 03:54.600
Oh, no. She says, I'm becoming small again.
 
03:54.700 --> 03:57.000
What's happening to me?

03:57.110 --> 04:03.230
Alice is small again and she suddenly falls into a pool of water.

04:03.240 --> 04:06.750
I'm in the sea. She thinks.

04:06.860 --> 04:08.710
But it is not the sea.

04:08.800 --> 04:11.600
It is the pool of Alice's tears.

04:11.710 --> 04:14.950
She sees a mouse swimming near her.

04:14.960 --> 04:17.940
Hello, Mouse. Says Alice.
 
04:17.950 --> 04:19.500
I'm tired.

04:19.600 --> 04:22.360
I want to get out of this pool.

04:22.420 --> 04:24.910
The mouse does not answer.

04:25.060 --> 04:30.110
Perhaps it doesn't understand English. Alice thinks.
 
04:30.520 --> 04:33.070
Maybe it understands French.

04:33.080 --> 04:38.270
Ooh, a machete? (Where is my cat?) asks Alice.
   
04:38.320 --> 04:41.500
This is the first sentence in her French book.

04:41.600 --> 04:46.890
The mouse is angry and says in English, I don't like cats.

04:47.000 --> 04:51.300
My family doesn't like cats. I'm a mouse.
 
04:51.410 --> 04:55.000
He swims away and Alice follows him.

04:58.000 --> 05:03.560
Chapter 2. The blue caterpillar.
 
05:04.560 --> 05:08.950
Soon, there are other strange animals in the pool.

05:08.960 --> 05:14.350
A duck, a Dodo, a parrot and a baby eagle.

05:14.360 --> 05:18.810
Alice gets out of the pool and the animals follow her.

05:18.900 --> 05:22.840
We're all wet. Says the Dodo.
 
05:22.950 --> 05:25.950
Let's run a race and get dry.

05:25.960 --> 05:29.760
That's a good idea. Says the parrot.
 
05:29.960 --> 05:33.960
Alice and the animals run a race and they get dry.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.700
After the race, the duck asks.

05:36.800 --> 05:38.900
Who wins this race?

05:39.100 --> 05:45.400
Everyone wins and everyone gets a prize. Says the Dodo.
 
05:45.540 --> 05:49.160
And Alice is giving the prizes.

05:49.210 --> 05:53.620
But I haven't got any prizes, Alice thinks.

05:53.700 --> 05:56.500
Alice does not know what to do.

05:56.610 --> 06:01.460
She puts her hand in her pocket and finds a box of sweets.

06:01.500 --> 06:05.390
Here are some sweets for everyone. She says. 

06:05.400 --> 06:08.560
She gives one sweet to every animal.

06:08.600 --> 06:12.520
Alice must have a prize too, says the Mouse.
 
06:12.550 --> 06:15.620
Of course, the Dodo says.
 
06:15.630 --> 06:18.630
What have you got for a prize, Alice?

06:18.740 --> 06:22.450
I've only got this box. Says Alice.

06:22.500 --> 06:25.620
And she gives him the empty sweet box.

06:25.680 --> 06:27.820
Good. Says the Dodo.
   
06:27.850 --> 06:32.670
Here's your prize, Alice - a beautiful box.
 
06:32.700 --> 06:36.250
How strange. She thinks.
  
06:36.300 --> 06:40.230
She looks at the Dodo and says, thank you.

06:40.280 --> 06:44.780
The animals go away and Alice is alone.

06:44.820 --> 06:48.400
She hears a noise and sees the White Rabbit.

06:48.510 --> 06:52.490
The Duchess. Says the White Rabbit.
  
06:52.510 --> 06:55.150
She's going to be angry.

06:55.360 --> 06:57.900
Where are my gloves?

06:57.910 --> 06:59.640
Alice looks around.

06:59.750 --> 07:04.430
Suddenly everything is different and she is in the countryside.

07:04.540 --> 07:08.130
The White Rabbit sees Alice and says.

07:08.140 --> 07:10.930
What are you doing here, Mary Ann?

07:11.000 --> 07:14.120
Run home and bring me my white gloves.

07:14.230 --> 07:18.610
He thinks I'm his servant. Thinks Alice.
  
07:18.700 --> 07:23.150
She runs to the White Rabbit's house and gets his gloves.

07:23.220 --> 07:27.450
Then she sees a bottle on a table and thinks.

07:27.640 --> 07:33.500
Every time I eat or drink something here, interesting things happen.

07:33.640 --> 07:37.170
She drinks it and starts to grow.

07:37.200 --> 07:43.115
She is now very big and puts one hand out of the window of the house.

07:43.240 --> 07:48.050
Mary Ann, where are you? Asks the White Rabbit.

07:48.060 --> 07:50.010
Where are my gloves?

07:50.060 --> 07:52.980
He tries to open the door of his house.

07:53.000 --> 07:56.750
But he can't because Alice's arm is against it.

07:56.800 --> 08:02.150
The White Rabbit calls his gardener. Pat. Pat.
  
08:02.160 --> 08:03.830
Where are you?

08:04.000 --> 08:07.150
I'm here, sir. Says Pat.
 
08:07.160 --> 08:12.150
There are other animals near the house and they want to help the White Rabbit.

08:12.160 --> 08:16.800
Come and help me. Says the White Rabbit angrily.
  
08:17.000 --> 08:19.650
What's that in the window, Pat?

08:19.700 --> 08:23.150
It's a hand. Says Pat.
 
08:23.160 --> 08:26.150
A hand? Says the White Rabbit.
 
08:26.760 --> 08:28.150
What are you saying?

08:28.160 --> 08:29.300
Listen to me.

08:29.870 --> 08:32.150
We must burn the house.

08:32.160 --> 08:35.360
What? Shouts Alice.
  
08:35.860 --> 08:38.150
The animals are silent for a moment.

08:38.160 --> 08:41.950
Then they throw stones through the windows.

08:42.000 --> 08:44.350
The stones become little cakes.

08:44.940 --> 08:48.450
Alice eats some of them and becomes small.

08:48.860 --> 08:52.000
She is happy and runs out of the house.

08:52.060 --> 08:57.840
The animals try to catch her, but she runs away into the wood.

08:57.950 --> 09:00.950
Alice sees a big mushroom in the wood.

09:01.060 --> 09:04.980
On top of the mushroom, there is a sleepy caterpillar.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.540
He is smoking a long pipe.

09:07.700 --> 09:12.050
Who are you? He asks quietly.
 
09:12.260 --> 09:16.830
I... I don't know. Says Alice.
 
09:16.940 --> 09:19.670
My size changes all the time.

09:19.680 --> 09:21.850
Now I'm very small.

09:21.960 --> 09:24.250
I don't understand.

09:24.260 --> 09:26.150
Says the blue caterpillar.

09:26.160 --> 09:30.150
I can't explain. Says Alice.

09:30.160 --> 09:32.900
Let me give you an example.

09:32.950 --> 09:36.700
One day, you're going to become a butterfly.

09:36.800 --> 09:38.800
That's strange, isn't it? 
  
09:38.900 --> 09:44.270
No. That's not strange at all. Says the caterpillar.
 
09:44.300 --> 09:47.150
But who are you?

09:47.160 --> 09:52.560
I want to know who you are first. Says Alice.
 
09:52.600 --> 09:55.850
Why? Ask the caterpillar.
  
09:55.960 --> 09:58.630
Alice can't answer the question.

09:58.800 --> 10:01.420
She is angry and walks away.

10:01.570 --> 10:04.350
Come back. Says the caterpillar.
  
10:04.460 --> 10:07.700
I want to tell you something.

10:07.920 --> 10:12.150
Alice goes back to the caterpillar and looks at him.

10:12.160 --> 10:17.100
You must never be angry. He says.
 
10:17.210 --> 10:21.700
Is that all? Asks Alice angrily.
 
10:21.800 --> 10:24.700
No. Says the caterpillar.
 
10:24.800 --> 10:29.150
He smokes his pipe and then gets off the mushroom.

10:29.160 --> 10:33.760
One side of this mushroom makes you big.

10:33.800 --> 10:38.550
And the other side makes you small.

10:38.660 --> 10:42.150
Alice looks at the mushroom and thinks,

10:42.160 --> 10:46.150
What side of the mushroom have I got to eat?

10:46.260 --> 10:51.800
She takes a piece from each side and then eats the first piece.

10:51.900 --> 10:55.150
Suddenly she grows very small.

10:55.160 --> 10:59.190
She eats the other piece and her neck grows long.

10:59.220 --> 11:11.150
Then she eats another piece and she becomes the right size. Now, she is happy.
 
11:11.160 --> 11:16.150
Chapter 3. The Cheshire Cat.

11:16.160 --> 11:18.450
Alice walks in the woods.

11:18.500 --> 11:22.150
She sees a nice garden and a small house.

11:22.160 --> 11:25.150
I'm too big. She thinks.
  
11:25.160 --> 11:27.720
I can't get into that house.

11:27.840 --> 11:32.150
I must eat a piece of mushroom and become small again.

11:32.160 --> 11:35.670
Soon she is nine inches tall.

11:35.750 --> 11:41.700
Suddenly a servant comes out of the wood and goes to the small house.

11:41.760 --> 11:44.150
His face is like a fish.

11:44.160 --> 11:49.150
Another servant opens the door and his face is like a frog.

11:49.160 --> 11:54.050
The fish servant has got a big letter in his hand and says, 
 
11:54.100 --> 12:04.150
For the Duchess. An invitation from the Queen to play croquet.

12:04.160 --> 12:14.150
The frog servant says, From the Queen. An invitation for the Duchess to play croquet.

12:14.160 --> 12:20.540
What strange servants! Says Alice, laughing.
 
12:20.640 --> 12:26.150
Alice goes to the house and says, Can I come in?
 
12:26.160 --> 12:31.550
Just open the door and go in. Says the servant.
 
12:31.600 --> 12:34.150
Then she sees the Duchess.

12:34.160 --> 12:38.790
She is sitting on a small chair with a baby in her arms.

12:38.810 --> 12:40.900
There is a cook in the kitchen.

12:41.000 --> 12:43.150
She is making some soup.

12:43.160 --> 12:46.480
There is too much pepper in the soup.

12:46.500 --> 12:50.150
Alice thinks and she sneezes. Achoo!
 
12:50.160 --> 12:54.680
Then the Duchess sneezes. Achoo!
  
12:54.720 --> 12:58.250
And the baby sneezes. Achoo!
 
12:58.360 --> 13:02.630
But the cook and a big cat do not sneeze.

13:02.740 --> 13:07.150
The cat sits near the cook and smiles.

13:07.160 --> 13:12.440
Alice asks the Duchess. Why does your cat smile?
  
13:12.500 --> 13:17.440
Because it's a Cheshire cat. Says the Duchess.
 
13:17.550 --> 13:21.800
All Cheshire cats smile, don't you know?

13:21.900 --> 13:25.150
No I don't. Says Alice.
 
13:25.160 --> 13:29.410
You don't know much. Says the Duchess.
 
13:29.500 --> 13:36.760
Suddenly the cook starts throwing plates, cups and pots at the Duchess and the baby.

13:36.810 --> 13:40.350
There is a terrible noise and Alice is afraid.

13:40.400 --> 13:43.740
Oh please be careful. Says Alice.
  
13:43.800 --> 13:45.630
The poor baby.

13:45.740 --> 13:50.000
Don't think about the baby. Says the Duchess.
 
13:50.100 --> 13:52.150
It's mine.

13:52.160 --> 13:54.890
She starts singing to the baby.

13:54.920 --> 13:58.150
But suddenly she throws it to Alice.

13:58.160 --> 14:01.150
Here. Take the baby.
 
14:01.160 --> 14:07.150
She says, I must go and play croquet with the Queen.

14:07.160 --> 14:09.440
She runs out of the house.

14:09.460 --> 14:14.110
The cook throws a plate at her but it does not hit her.

14:14.120 --> 14:16.540
Alice goes outside with a baby.

14:16.650 --> 14:19.150
It makes strange noises.

14:19.160 --> 14:22.150
Alice looks at it carefully.

14:22.160 --> 14:24.540
It is a baby pig.

14:24.660 --> 14:29.050
A pig? Says Alice, surprised.
  
14:29.100 --> 14:33.800
She puts it down immediately and it runs into the wood.

14:33.900 --> 14:38.150
Just then Alice sees the Cheshire cat in a tree.

14:38.160 --> 14:41.150
It looks at Alice and smiles.

14:41.160 --> 14:45.150
Hello Cheshire cat. Says Alice.
 
14:45.160 --> 14:47.150
Where can I go now?

14:47.160 --> 14:53.150
Well, where do you want to go? Asks the Cheshire cat.
 
14:53.160 --> 14:56.940
I, I don't know. Says Alice.
  
14:57.000 --> 15:03.700
You can go that way on the right and you can visit the hatter. Says the Cheshire cat.
 
15:03.800 --> 15:09.590
Or you can go that way on the left and you can visit the March Hare.

15:09.600 --> 15:13.150
It doesn't matter. They're both mad.
   
15:13.160 --> 15:15.950
Oh dear. Says Alice.
  
15:16.000 --> 15:18.770
I don't want to visit mad people.

15:18.800 --> 15:23.450
Then you're in the wrong place. Says the Cheshire cat.
  
15:23.500 --> 15:27.500
We're all mad here. You're mad too.
  
15:27.710 --> 15:30.950
How do you know I'm mad? Asks Alice.
 
15:31.000 --> 15:34.000
You're here. Says the Cheshire cat.
  
15:34.160 --> 15:36.580
So of course you're mad.

15:36.710 --> 15:42.520
Are you going to play croquet with the Queen today? Asks the Cheshire cat.
 
15:42.600 --> 15:47.450
No. I haven't got an invitation. Says Alice.
  
15:47.500 --> 15:51.150
I'm going to be there. Says the Cheshire cat.
  
15:51.160 --> 15:54.150
And he suddenly goes away.

15:54.160 --> 15:58.620
Then he comes back and asks. Where's the baby?
  
15:58.740 --> 16:03.150
It's not a baby. Says Alice. It's a pig.
   
16:03.160 --> 16:07.610
Oh. He says and goes away again.
 
16:07.740 --> 16:12.160
Alice goes to the March Hare's house.

16:12.700 --> 16:16.590
What a big house. Alice thinks.
 
16:16.610 --> 16:18.580
But I'm very small.

16:19.100 --> 16:23.250
She eats another piece of mushroom and she becomes big.

16:27.000 --> 16:30.280
Chapter 4. The Tea Party.
   
16:32.000 --> 16:34.750
There is a big table in front of the house.

16:34.860 --> 16:38.500
The March Hare and the Hatter are having tea.

16:38.610 --> 16:41.600
The doormouse is on the table between them.

16:41.700 --> 16:45.910
When the March Hare and the Hatter see Alice, they say.

16:46.000 --> 16:48.150
There's no room. No room.
  
16:48.160 --> 16:52.500
But there's a lot of room. Says Alice.
 
16:52.660 --> 16:55.150
And she sits in a big chair.

16:55.160 --> 16:58.150
The Hatter looks at his watch and asks.

16:58.160 --> 17:03.150
What day is it? I think it's Monday. Says Alice.
   
17:03.160 --> 17:07.150
My watch says Wednesday. Says the Hatter.
 
17:07.160 --> 17:10.150
The March Hare puts his watch in his tea.

17:10.160 --> 17:12.150
Alice is surprised.

17:12.160 --> 17:15.550
What's he doing? She thinks.
 
17:16.000 --> 17:19.590
Then the March Hare takes it out and looks at it.

17:20.160 --> 17:26.150
Alice looks at the March Hare's watch and says. What a strange watch.
 
17:26.160 --> 17:28.720
It shows the day of the month.

17:28.760 --> 17:31.150
But it doesn't show the time.

17:31.160 --> 17:35.540
Does your watch show the year? Asks the Hatter.
 
17:35.600 --> 17:38.390
Of course not. Says Alice.
   
17:38.500 --> 17:42.150
Because it's the same year for a long time.

17:42.160 --> 17:46.700
Well, it's the same with my watch. Says the Hatter.
 
17:46.780 --> 17:49.150
It's always six o'clock here.

17:49.160 --> 17:53.150
Have some more tea. Says the March Hare.
 
17:53.160 --> 17:57.700
Thank you. But I haven't got any tea. Says Alice.
   
17:57.800 --> 18:00.000
How can I have more?

18:00.100 --> 18:02.150
Oh. Says the Hatter.
  
18:02.160 --> 18:05.150
You can always have more than nothing.

18:05.160 --> 18:07.950
Alice is confused and angry.

18:08.000 --> 18:12.150
She gets up from the table and walks away through the trees.

18:12.160 --> 18:16.750
The Hatter tries to put the door mouse into the teapot.

18:17.000 --> 18:21.150
What a stupid tea party. She thinks.
 
18:21.160 --> 18:25.840
Alice is walking in the wood and sees a door in a tree.

18:26.000 --> 18:30.600
She opens it and sees the hall with a glass table again.

18:31.160 --> 18:36.150
This time I want to go into the garden. She thinks.
 
18:36.160 --> 18:39.530
She takes the key and opens the door.

18:39.700 --> 18:43.550
She eats a piece of mushroom and becomes small.

18:43.700 --> 18:49.700
Then she walks into the beautiful garden with lovely flowers and fountains.

18:50.000 --> 18:55.840
There is a big rose tree near the door of the garden and she sees three gardeners.

18:55.900 --> 18:57.450
But they are not men.

18:57.700 --> 19:03.420
They are playing cards and each of them has got a head, hands and feet.

19:03.500 --> 19:06.850
They are painting the white roses red.

19:07.160 --> 19:10.150
Alice sees them and says, Hello.

19:10.160 --> 19:12.150
My name is Alice.

19:12.160 --> 19:15.600
Why are you painting the roses red?

19:15.700 --> 19:20.050
The Queen hates white roses. Says five.
 
19:20.100 --> 19:23.680
She only likes red roses. Says seven.
 
19:23.720 --> 19:30.150
We must paint them red or she's going to cut off our heads. Says two.
 
19:30.160 --> 19:36.150
Cut off your heads. Says Alice, surprised.
 
19:36.160 --> 19:42.670
Suddenly one of the cards says, Look, it's the Queen, the Queen.

19:42.760 --> 19:46.550
Alice turns around and sees a lot of people.

19:46.600 --> 19:51.770
They are all playing cards, each with a head, hands and feet.

19:51.820 --> 20:01.160
There are soldiers with clubs, servants with diamonds and spades, children with hearts and kings and queens.

20:05.000 --> 20:08.150
A drink called tea.

20:08.160 --> 20:10.150
What is tea?

20:10.160 --> 20:16.150
Tea comes from the dry leaves of the Camellia Synensis plant.

20:16.160 --> 20:21.820
This plant grows in high places with hot weather and a lot of rain.

20:21.840 --> 20:28.150
There are three types of tea, black, green and oolong.

20:28.160 --> 20:31.150
Where does tea come from?

20:31.160 --> 20:36.150
Most tea comes from India, China and Sri Lanka.

20:36.160 --> 20:44.150
But some comes from Africa, Malaysia, Indonesia, Japan and South America.

20:44.160 --> 20:48.150
Today tea grows in about 40 countries.

20:48.160 --> 20:53.150
Look at the map and find the countries.

20:53.160 --> 20:56.150
Tea around the world.

20:56.160 --> 20:59.150
The British like drinking tea.

20:59.160 --> 21:04.150
In the afternoon they sometimes have cakes and sandwiches with it.

21:04.160 --> 21:13.160
This is called afternoon tea and it means both the drink and the food, like in the picture on page 38.

21:14.160 --> 21:20.150
Some big hotels have got tea rooms where people go to talk and enjoy a cup of tea.

21:20.160 --> 21:25.150
You can also get afternoon tea in most cafes.

21:25.160 --> 21:30.150
The Japanese have a tea ceremony called Cha Noyu.

21:30.160 --> 21:33.450
They drink their tea in a special tea house.

21:33.470 --> 21:37.100
Everything is important in this ceremony.

21:37.160 --> 21:43.150
The tea, the teapot, the cups and the teaspoons.

21:43.160 --> 21:51.150
In North Africa and the Middle East people drink strong hot tea in small glasses with sugar.

21:51.160 --> 21:56.150
In some countries of North Africa people drink green tea and mint.

21:56.160 --> 21:58.580
It is a good drink in hot weather.

22:00.160 --> 22:05.150
In Turkey people drink tea in special glasses with cubes of sugar.

22:05.160 --> 22:11.150
They drink more tea in Turkey than in any other country.

22:11.160 --> 22:15.150
Russian people use a samovar to make tea.

22:15.160 --> 22:23.150
A samovar has got a lot of hot water so the Russians can drink tea all day.

22:23.160 --> 22:29.150
You can drink tea hot or cold with milk or with lemon.

22:29.160 --> 22:36.150
A lot of doctors say tea is good for you.

22:36.160 --> 22:40.000
Chapter 5, Croquet

22:41.160 --> 22:45.150
The Queen stops and looks at Alice.

22:45.160 --> 22:50.150
What's your name, child? asks the Queen.
 
22:50.160 --> 22:53.150
My name's Alice, she says.

22:53.160 --> 22:58.750
Then she thinks, I mustn't be afraid. They're only cards.

22:59.060 --> 23:06.150
The Queen looks at the gardeners and asks, And who are they?
 
23:06.160 --> 23:10.150
Don't ask me, says Alice. I don't know.
 
23:10.160 --> 23:18.150
The Queen is very angry with Alice and says, Cut off her head!
 
23:18.160 --> 23:21.150
The King looks at the Queen and says,

23:21.160 --> 23:24.750
But she's only a child, dear.

23:24.860 --> 23:27.760
The Queen is now angry with the gardeners.

23:28.000 --> 23:31.140
Cut off their heads!

23:31.160 --> 23:35.150
She says to the soldiers, the gardeners are afraid.

23:35.160 --> 23:42.150
Alice, Alice! They shout. Please help us.
 
23:42.160 --> 23:46.100
Come here fast, says Alice.

23:46.120 --> 23:50.050
She puts them in a flower pot and no one can see them.

23:50.100 --> 23:55.150
Are their heads off? asks the Queen.
  
23:55.160 --> 23:59.150
The soldiers can't see the cards.

23:59.160 --> 24:03.900
Their heads are gone. Say the soldiers.
 
24:04.100 --> 24:06.850
That's good, says the Queen.

24:07.000 --> 24:10.150
Now let's play Croquet.

24:10.160 --> 24:13.150
Can you play Croquet, dear?

24:13.160 --> 24:19.150
Yes, says Alice. Come on then! Says the Queen.
  
24:19.660 --> 24:23.920
Alice walks away with the Queen, the King and the others.

24:24.000 --> 24:28.650
Go to your places! Shouts the Queen.
 
24:29.160 --> 24:32.150
Let's start the game!

24:32.160 --> 24:35.750
What a funny game! Alice thinks.
  
24:36.000 --> 24:40.150
The balls are hedgehogs and the mallets are flamingos.

24:40.160 --> 24:43.150
It's going to be difficult.

24:43.160 --> 24:49.150
During the game, the Queen is often angry and shouts, Cut off his head!
 
24:49.160 --> 24:51.150
Cut off her head!

24:51.160 --> 24:54.500
Oh dear. Alice thinks.
 
24:54.600 --> 24:57.150
What's going to happen to my head?

24:57.160 --> 25:01.020
Suddenly Alice sees the Cheshire Cat.

25:01.160 --> 25:02.930
She is happy to see him.

25:03.500 --> 25:07.150
How are you, dear? asks the Cheshire Cat.
 
25:07.160 --> 25:10.750
I don't like this game. Says Alice.
 
25:10.860 --> 25:14.920
No one knows how to play and everyone is angry.

25:15.000 --> 25:18.800
Do you like the Queen? asks the Cheshire Cat.
 
25:19.160 --> 25:22.030
No, I don't. Says Alice.
  
25:22.160 --> 25:25.150
The King sees Alice and the Cheshire Cat.

25:25.160 --> 25:29.550
Who are you talking to? He asks.
 
25:29.660 --> 25:33.750
It's my friend, the Cheshire Cat. Says Alice.
 
25:34.000 --> 25:37.100
I don't like it. Says the King.
 
25:37.160 --> 25:41.150
But it can kiss my hand.

25:41.160 --> 25:45.150
No, thank you! Says the Cheshire Cat.
 
25:45.160 --> 25:48.200
The King is angry and calls the Queen.

25:48.350 --> 25:52.150
My dear. Take this cat away.
 
25:52.160 --> 25:57.150
Of course. Says the Queen. Cut off its head!
  
25:57.160 --> 26:00.150
Everyone looks at the Cheshire Cat.

26:00.160 --> 26:02.150
A soldier says.

26:02.160 --> 26:06.640
I can't cut off its head because it hasn't got a body.

26:06.700 --> 26:10.680
It's got a head. Says the King angrily.
 
26:10.720 --> 26:12.150
Cut it off.

26:12.160 --> 26:18.150
It's the Duchess's Cheshire Cat. Says Alice. Ask her.
  
26:18.160 --> 26:20.580
The Duchess is in prison.

26:20.600 --> 26:25.150
Bring her here. Says the Queen to a soldier.
 
26:25.160 --> 26:28.160
Suddenly, the Cheshire Cat goes away.

26:32.160 --> 26:35.160
Chapter 6. The Trial.

26:36.160 --> 26:39.150
Suddenly, someone shouts.

26:39.160 --> 26:42.850
The trail's beginning. The trail's beginning.

26:43.160 --> 26:47.850
A trail? asks Alice. Whose trail is it?
  
26:48.000 --> 26:50.150
But no one answers Alice.

26:50.160 --> 26:52.750
She is soon in the courtroom.

26:52.800 --> 26:57.150
The King and Queen of Hearts are sitting on their thrones.

26:57.160 --> 27:00.550
The nave of hearts is standing in front of them.

27:00.600 --> 27:05.580
There are a lot of birds, animals and cards sitting in the courtroom.

27:05.640 --> 27:10.150
In the middle, there is a table with a big plate of tarts on it.

27:10.160 --> 27:16.150
The White Rabbit is near the King with a long piece of paper in his hand.

27:16.160 --> 27:18.150
He starts reading.

27:18.160 --> 27:24.450
The Queen of Hearts, she makes some tarts all on a summer day.

27:24.660 --> 27:29.660
But the nave of hearts, he takes the tarts away.

27:30.000 --> 27:33.540
Cut off his head! Shouts the Queen.
 
27:33.600 --> 27:36.520
Oh no! Says the White Rabbit.
 
27:36.600 --> 27:40.150
We've got to listen to some witnesses first.

27:40.160 --> 27:43.650
Very well. Says the King.
  
27:43.760 --> 27:46.150
Call the first witness.

27:46.160 --> 27:49.650
The first witness is the Hatter.

27:49.760 --> 27:54.650
He has got a teacup in one hand and bread and butter in the other.

27:54.760 --> 27:59.750
I'm sorry about this, but it's my tea time. Says the Hatter.
 
27:59.860 --> 28:03.150
Oh really? Says the King.
 
28:03.160 --> 28:05.150
Take off your hat.

28:05.160 --> 28:08.400
It isn't mine. Says the Hatter.
 
28:08.420 --> 28:12.630
Whose hat is it then? Asks the King angrily.
  
28:12.760 --> 28:16.150
I don't know. Says the Hatter.
 
28:16.160 --> 28:18.150
I sell hats.

28:18.160 --> 28:21.100
Tell me what you know. Says the King.
 
28:21.120 --> 28:25.150
Oh, I don't know anything. Says the Hatter.
 
28:25.160 --> 28:28.150
The Queen looks at the Hatter with her glasses.

28:28.160 --> 28:31.920
He is afraid of her and his face is white.

28:32.000 --> 28:36.150
He bites a piece of his teacup instead of his bread and butter.

28:36.160 --> 28:41.110
I'm just a poor man. Says the Hatter sadly.
 
28:41.160 --> 28:44.650
Please let me go and finish my tea.

28:45.000 --> 28:49.150
Very well. You can go. Says the King.
  
28:49.160 --> 28:52.150
Can't off his head outside?

28:52.160 --> 28:54.600
The Queen says to one of the soldiers.

28:54.700 --> 28:58.750
But the Hatter runs away quickly and no one can catch him.

28:59.000 --> 29:02.150
Suddenly Alice feels strange.

29:02.160 --> 29:06.720
Oh no. She thinks. I'm growing again.
 
29:07.000 --> 29:11.150
Call the next witness. Shouts the King.
  
29:11.160 --> 29:14.150
The next witness is the Duchess's cook.

29:14.160 --> 29:20.150
She comes into the courtroom with a big pepper pot and everyone sneezes.

29:20.160 --> 29:24.750
Tell me everything you know. Says the King.
 
29:24.800 --> 29:27.150
No. Says the cook.
 
29:27.160 --> 29:31.150
The King is surprised and looks at the White Rabbit.

29:31.160 --> 29:34.860
Ask the witness questions your majesty.

29:34.920 --> 29:37.150
Says the White Rabbit quietly.

29:37.160 --> 29:40.150
Oh. That's right. Says the King.
  
29:40.300 --> 29:44.150
What are tarts made of?

29:44.160 --> 29:48.150
The Maid of Pepper. Answers the cook.

29:48.160 --> 29:53.550
The Maid of Sugar. Says the Sleepy Door Mouse.
 
29:53.560 --> 29:55.610
What? Says the Queen.
 
29:55.630 --> 29:59.650
Send the door mouse away. Can't off its head.
 
29:59.700 --> 30:02.350
There is a lot of noise in the courtroom.

30:02.460 --> 30:05.150
And at last the door mouse goes away.

30:05.160 --> 30:10.080
Call the next witness. Says the King.
 
30:10.100 --> 30:16.150
The White Rabbit looks at his long piece of paper and says... Alice.
 
30:16.160 --> 30:20.850
Alice is very surprised. She is quite big now.
 
30:21.000 --> 30:25.860
She stands up quickly and some of the birds and animals fall over.

30:26.000 --> 30:29.750
Oh. Says Alice. I'm very sorry.
  
30:29.800 --> 30:33.420
Then she goes and stands in front of the King and Queen.

30:34.000 --> 30:38.150
What do you know about this? Asks the King.
 
30:38.160 --> 30:40.450
Nothing, answers Alice.

30:40.500 --> 30:44.600
That's very important. Says the King.
 
30:45.000 --> 30:49.470
You mean unimportant to your majesty. Says the White Rabbit.

30:49.600 --> 30:52.050
Of course. Says the King.
 
30:52.100 --> 30:55.150
I mean unimportant.

30:55.160 --> 30:58.350
Then he writes something in a book.

31:02.160 --> 31:04.200
A Real Queen.

31:06.000 --> 31:12.150
Her name is Elizabeth Alexandra Mary Windsor.

31:12.160 --> 31:19.150
Her date of birth is the 21st of April 1926.

31:19.160 --> 31:26.150
She becomes Queen on the 27th of May 1952.

31:26.160 --> 31:30.600
Her title is Queen Elizabeth II.

31:31.000 --> 31:37.150
She is Queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland.

31:37.160 --> 31:42.150
Her husband is Philip Duke of Edinburgh.

31:42.160 --> 31:51.150
She has got three sons, Charles, Andrew and Edward and one daughter, Anne.

31:51.160 --> 31:55.150
She has got eight grandchildren.

31:55.160 --> 32:01.150
She loves dogs, especially corgis.

32:01.160 --> 32:07.150
She loves horses and she loves horse riding.

32:07.160 --> 32:12.150
When she is in London, she lives in Buckingham Palace.

32:12.160 --> 32:20.150
Her other homes are Windsor Castle near London and Sandringham House in the east of England.

32:20.160 --> 32:25.150
She has got a castle in Scotland, Balmoral Castle.

32:25.160 --> 32:28.750
She goes here for her summer holidays.

32:32.000 --> 32:37.150
Chapter 7. Back home for tea.

32:37.160 --> 32:40.150
Silence in the courtroom.

32:40.160 --> 32:41.700
Shouts the King.

32:42.000 --> 32:45.670
I have got an important rule for you.

32:46.000 --> 32:49.150
Everyone is silent and looks at the King.

32:49.160 --> 32:51.800
He opens a book and reads.

32:52.000 --> 32:54.150
Rule 42.

32:54.160 --> 33:00.150
All people, more than a mile tall, must leave the courtroom.

33:00.160 --> 33:03.150
Everyone looks at Alice.

33:03.160 --> 33:06.640
I'm not a mile tall. Says Alice.
 
33:06.800 --> 33:09.150
Yes you are. Says the King.
 
33:09.160 --> 33:14.150
You're more than two miles tall. Says the Queen.
 
33:14.160 --> 33:17.500
I don't want to leave the courtroom. Says Alice.
 
33:17.580 --> 33:19.800
It's not a real rule.

33:19.900 --> 33:24.150
It's a very old rule. Says the King.
 
33:24.160 --> 33:30.450
Then why is it rule 42 and not rule one? Ask Alice.

33:31.000 --> 33:35.150
The King does not know what to say and closes the book quickly.

33:35.160 --> 33:38.150
The White Rabbit jumps up and says.

33:38.160 --> 33:40.930
Look, I've got a letter.

33:41.000 --> 33:44.010
He puts his glasses on and looks at it.

33:44.250 --> 33:50.150
Oh, it's not a letter. It's a poem. He says.
   
33:50.160 --> 33:56.150
Read it from the beginning and stop at the end. Says the King.
 
33:56.160 --> 34:01.150
The White Rabbit reads the poem, but no one understands it.

34:01.160 --> 34:04.700
This poem is nonsense. Says Alice.
 
34:04.720 --> 34:08.700
Oh, cut off the naves hit. Says the Queen.
  
34:09.000 --> 34:12.000
What nonsense? Shouts Alice.
  
34:12.100 --> 34:16.500
She is not afraid of anyone now because she is very big.

34:16.520 --> 34:19.550
Be quiet. Shouts the Queen.
 
34:19.560 --> 34:21.720
No. Shouts Alice.
 
34:21.800 --> 34:25.800
The Queen is very angry and her face is purple.

34:25.820 --> 34:29.400
Cut off her hand. She shouts.
 
34:29.500 --> 34:32.520
I'm not afraid of you. Says Alice.
 
34:32.550 --> 34:34.850
You're only cards.

34:34.870 --> 34:39.780
Suddenly the cards fly up into the air and fall down on her.

34:39.800 --> 34:42.600
Oh dear. Says Alice.
 
34:42.620 --> 34:45.150
She pushes the cards away from her face.

34:45.660 --> 34:47.150
Alice wakes up.

34:47.160 --> 34:49.150
These cards are leaves.

34:49.160 --> 34:52.150
Her sister pushes them away from her face.

34:52.160 --> 34:56.150
Wake up Alice dear. Says her sister.
 
34:56.160 --> 35:01.150
Oh. What a strange dream. Says Alice.
 
35:01.160 --> 35:05.150
Please tell me about it. Says her sister.
  
35:05.160 --> 35:08.150
Alice tells her sister about the dream.

35:08.160 --> 35:11.150
Her sister listens and then laughs.

35:11.160 --> 35:14.150
Haha. Yes. She says.
 
35:14.160 --> 35:16.450
It's a very strange dream.

35:16.560 --> 35:20.160
But it's late now and it's time for your tea.

35:21.160 --> 35:34.150
Alice runs home and thinks about the White Rabbit, the caterpillar, the duchess, the hatter, the Cheshire cat, the croquet game, the queen, the king and the cards.

35:34.160 --> 35:38.150
What a wonderful dream. She says happily.
 
35:38.160 --> 35:43.160
One day I can tell my children about it.
